2026-09-27T12:07:40.5351957Z Description:
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5352514Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5353010Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5354288Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5355582Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5355724Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5355956Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5356273Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5356548Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5356692Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5356926Z ================
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5357039Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5357491Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5358008Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5358227Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5358477Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5358779Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5358951Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5359127Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5359565Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5359955Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5360615Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5361116Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5361248Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5361720Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5362275Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5362547Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5362866Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5363263Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5363394Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5363645Z ========
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5363761Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5365014Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5366290Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5366532Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5367030Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5368226Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5368875Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5369464Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5369931Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5370339Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5370485Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5370778Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5370933Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5371986Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5373097Z 
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5373748Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5374649Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:07:40.5445284Z 
